        "insufficient_evidence": false,
        "summary": "Adams warned against choosing an idea you lack real passion for—or one that is merely useful but doesn’t excite people.",
        "summary_citation_ids": [
          "S1"
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "heading": "The mistake to avoid",
            "content": "He said founders need personal passion to carry them through the difficult periods. And a product shouldn’t just be useful: it should delight people enough that they want to sign up, pay for it, and tell others about it. Adams also said Canva built for itself because its founders were its customers, while noting that this worked because they experienced problems shared by many people.",
            "citation_ids": [
